    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0166" n="78" xml:id="pg78"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.001 W 64/46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor for the Department of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Polk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-06">December 6,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Phillips</hi>: I spoke to the President about
                    this matter,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d67-f1"/> and he said under no circumstances
                    was he prepared to commit himself at this time. The question of the punishment
                    of the German Kaiser could be taken up when he reached France.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rank</hi>] L[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >yon</hi>] P[<hi rendition="#small-caps">olk</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d67-f1" n="5" xml:id="d67-f1-content">
                <p>See memorandum from the British Embassy, <ref target="frus1919v02#pg_653">
